WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:02.702
- Sometimes when guys talk about,
 you know, when they realize

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:04.704
they have the respect of their peers,
they felt vindicated.

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:07.507
They can remember, like, a specific guy

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:11.211
saying something to them, and they said,
"Oh, when he knew I was nice,

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:13.113
- Wow.
- I knew I was nice."

00:00:13.113 --> 00:00:14.814
- That's a great—that's…

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:17.384
- Is there someone like that for you?
- Yeah.

00:00:17.384 --> 00:00:19.386
And it's crazy. Just crazy. That's…

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:22.489
One person who

00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:25.625
my rookie year told me something
that stuck with me—

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:29.329
I don't even know if he remember
this—is Michael Redd.

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:34.901
He told me I was gonna be special
in this league. Keep, keep,

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:37.537
don't stop. Like,

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:39.873
I just remember those words so vividly.

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:45.011
You gonna be special in this league.
Don't stop. Keep working. It was my rookie year,
Michael Redd.

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:48.181
I never got the chance to tell him
thank you for that. He might,

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:50.817
he may not even remember.
- Yeah.
- But Michael Redd

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:54.621
told me those words,
 and it stuck with me to this day.
- Really?

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:58.591
Why do you think in that moment, like, that
was so, it resonated so deeply for you?

00:00:59.025 --> 00:01:01.828
- I don't know. At that time, you know,

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:02.729
he was a veteran.

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:04.831
You know, he was an established player.

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:08.635
He was a player, like, I've always been
a fan of the game of basketball.

00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:11.171
'70s, '80s, '90s.

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:15.075
So I always respected
all the older guys.
- Mmhmm.
- Honest.

00:01:15.108 --> 00:01:17.977
I respected what Michael Redd did
in the league.

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:20.280
And I don't know.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:21.681
It was just that moment where he pulled me

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:25.985
to the side and, you know,
I felt how genuine he was about it,

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:29.456
you know what I mean? Because even at that point,
my rookie year, you know,

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:33.460
you deal with so many emotions

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:37.730
questioning, like, damn, "When am I gonna be good?
When Imma be able to be myself

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:40.767
and be comfortable?" Like, I'm
only 19 years old playing with grown men.

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:44.671
So for him to pull me to the side
and acknowledge something

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:48.875
towards me that I was feeling
iffy about was all I needed.

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:51.678
- Shoutout Michael Redd.
- Shoutout Michael Redd.
- I love that.

